  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2025-11-27T02:35:01.312Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "deletedBy": null,
  "details": "The Matcap rendering in VRC’s Toon Standard shader appears to be incorrect.\n\nWhen the object is viewed from directly above, the Matcap texture collapses toward a single point, creating a noticeable distortion.\n\nThis behavior can also be observed in the Liltoon shader, but it doesn’t seem desirable from a shading or usability standpoint.\n\nThe older VRC Matcap shader did not have this issue, as its spherical mapping handled polar regions more gracefully.\n\nI would appreciate it if this problem could be addressed and corrected.",
